{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381640-social-action-and-intimacy-reply-to-a-question-in-ask-the-devs-thread","id":1381640,"title":"Social action and intimacy (reply to a question in \"Ask the Devs\" thread)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T07:25:57-07:00","id":1381640,"title":"Social action and intimacy (reply to a question in \"Ask the Devs\" thread)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1381613#post1381613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple of questions about the social system, specifically about intimacies supporting social influence, which doesn't seem precisely explained (unless I can't find it).<br /> <br /> People often say you need &quot;tag&quot; a specific intimacy. Ie you need to say &quot;I'm using his intimacy of I Love Dragonblood to persuade him to help&quot;, you can't just throw a social influence and hope they've got something applicable. Or even that you can literally only do this when you actually know their Intimacy (via Profile Character or something). But I can't actually see that anywhere. It just says &quot;When a character is targeted by an influence roll that opposes one or more of his Intimacies, add a bonus to his Resolve based on the intensity of the most applicable Intimacy. On the other hand, if one or more of a character\u2019s Intimacies supports an influence roll applied against him, then he suffers a corresponding penalty to Resolve based on the most applicable Intimacy.&quot; And that &quot;Without exploiting an Intimacy, persuasion isn\u2019t possible.&quot; So I can't actually see anything that says you need to know what their intimacies are.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know the answer to your question. What you are looking for is pg. 216 &quot;Persuade&quot;. There it is explained:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The extent of the action you can compel with persuade depends on the Intimacies of your target.<br /> Without an Intimacy to support your influence roll, you can only convince others to take relatively trivial and riskfree actions\u2014begging a coin from a passing stranger is about the limit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13172-balwin","name":"balwin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:36:12-07:00","id":1381695,"title":"","content":"In other words, you can fire blindly and, without realizing it, hit someone &quot;where they live&quot; (ie: in a Defining Intimacy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:03:38-07:00","id":1381724,"title":"","content":"It's still better to make an educated guess. If someone's a butcher, it's pretty reasonable to assume that it'd be easier to convince them to sell their beef at a discount to draw customers away from another butcher, than it would be to persuade them to join your fight against the Wyld Hunt for the promise that their deeds will live on in song.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:33:37-07:00","id":1381736,"title":"","content":"Oh, absolutely, it's much more likely to work with an educated guess. But you never know. If you're a beggar hoping people are charitable or compassionate, you just try hundreds of people on the chance someone's going to have an appropriate intimacy.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I asked (though this is something that's come up repeatedly, where I've found my idea of how the social system works is not the same as others) is because a PC tried to Persuade another PC to not shoot some people dead, and wanted to tag an intimacy I didn't think was reasonable.<br /> <br /> But the PC who was shooting people had, I thought I remembered, some kind of intimacy of compassion or niceness or something. So I wondered if the talking PC's persuasion should work anyway based on his initial argument of &quot;please don't shoot those poor people&quot;, despite him not knowing she had that intimacy, or the player even saying &quot;I want to base this on her intimacy of compassion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Actually, in the end I found I'd remembered wrong, and she didn't have an intimacy of compassion, but it was something to consider for future reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}